750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) can opener blade (food debris);
B) tongs hanging above grill and by prep cooler (grease/food debris);
C) colander in mopsink (food debris);
D) prep cooler - pans in top used for cheese storage (food debris buildup);
E) hood filters (grease);   and
F) plastic tub used for extra chip storage (empty and contained food debris).

Food contact surfaces must be properly cleaned and sanitized between uses/as needed, up to every 4 hours after continuous use, to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris. Change out food pans for prep coolers daily. Take soiled tongs and other equipment to dish area at the end of operations day. Clean hood filters as needed between routine hood service. Colander in mopsink is typically used to catch straws and other items if mopsink is used as a dump sink. Do not use the colander for other purposes (i.e. food prep, etc.).

