findings.citation_text:
750.1220 - Floors were soiled in the following areas:
A) cook line behind grill and fryers (grease/food debris);
B) walkin cooler (food debris under shelving);
C) under 2 door cooler and stainless steel freezer (food/general debris);
D) corner/wall under 3 part sink in dish area (grimy buildup/general debris); 
E) beneath in-use soda syrup at bar (bottle caps/debris);   and
F) under ice machine/corner past ice machine (bottles caps/general debris stuck at gap in floor to wall juncture).

Clean floors throughout daily/as needed and maintain clean (see general comments for details on general maintenance).

750.1200 & 1220 - A) (R) Plastic baseboard is loose at the wall between the prep cooler and the grill. Grease and food debris accumulates in the area, but buildup was less than what was observed at the previous inspection. Clean the debris out from the aforementioned area and re-seal the baseboard to the wall. If it is difficult to keep baseboard attached to the wall then remove the baseboard and seal the floor to wall juncture with a durable, cleanable silicone or caulk. **NOTE: Baseboard is starting to pull loose along the top of the wall by the fryers as well**

B) Floors were soiled in the following areas:
1. (R) kitchen - heavily soiled with grease and food debris, especially under the cooking equipment, along the walls around cooking equipment, along the white PVC pipe between the wall and fryers, and next to the prep cooler; 
2. dish room - along walls, especially behind the dish machine (Decon pellets, utensils, food debris, & puddling water observed in openings of cinder blocks used to house dish machine);
3. walkin cooler - along wall beneath metal wire shelving (food debris);
4. bar - along walls in various spots (behind ice machine, under ice bin at east end of bar, etc.);  and
5. mop closet - around water heater and mopsink (Decon pellets, debris, cigarette butts).
Clean the floors throughout the facility as needed and maintain clean.

Floors must be in good repair, constructed to facilitate easy cleaning, and maintained. Junctures between walls and floors shall be coved and sealed.

